  "Number": 16,
  "Question": "Leap Day, February \\(29,\\) \\(2004,\\) occurred on a Sunday. On what day of the week will Leap Day, February \\(29,\\) \\(2020,\\) occur?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Tuesday",
    "B": "Wednesday",
    "C": "Thursday",
    "D": "Friday",
    "E": "Saturday"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Weekdays repeat every \\(7\\) days, so complete weeks do not change the weekday.\n\nThe successive Leap Days here occur in \\(2004,2008,2012,2016,2020\\). Between each pair of successive Leap Days there are four years of \\(365\\) days plus one extra February day, giving\n\\[\n4\\cdot365+1=1461\\text{ days}.\n\\]\nThere are four such intervals from \\(2004\\) to \\(2020\\), so the elapsed time is\n\\[\n4\\cdot1461=5844=7\\cdot834+6\\text{ days}.\n\\]\nThe weekday therefore advances \\(6\\) days. Six days after Sunday is \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
